{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:17c551b97f38be2f","name":"Behemoth Junk Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-17c551b97f38be2f","title":"Behemoth Junk Droid","revision":25612,"timestamp":"2024-11-29T01:59:04Z","sha256":"61f080be9060ac3afac0aee67a3d85595f6553fe8f89e7512737a3894415d287","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25612","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Behemoth%20Junk%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-17c551b97f38be2f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," ravaged the galaxy, the debris of battle built up at the same time, and material for high-tech items became scarce. Inevitably, numerous groups turned to recycling, repurposing, and just rebuilding broken bits of technology to suit their needs. This was particularly common on worlds ravaged by ground fighting in major cities, and worlds filled with junk, such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Raxus Prime"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Raxus_Prime","referenceId":"reference:9a3dfa77203e9cf1"},". When such jury-rigged efforts were turned to creating automatons, the results were cobbled-together \"Junk\" Droids.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although Junk Droids could conceivably be built out of any spare Droid and vehicle parts and set to any needed task, the majority fall into three broad groups: standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Junk Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Junk_Droids"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Brute Junk Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Brute_Junk_Droids"},", and Behemoth Junk Droids. Regular ",{"tag":"a","children":["Junk Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Junk_Droids"}," are approximately ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," size and shape and generally used for common labor tasks. Because they were fairly fragile, they were often equipped with a shield or blocking limb to help prevent damage in the course of their duties. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Brute Junk Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Brute_Junk_Droids"}," are larger and more likely to be quadrupeds, built to be strong and solid rather than flexible. They are used as beasts of burden and brute-force guards. Behemoth Junk Droids are always specialty-built, often to serve as walking power plants or armored carriers. Many have a storage space to carry a small creature safely within.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Because Junk Droids have mashed-together programming, they are considered dangerous by most civilized people. They might go on a rampage, confuse orders, or even start building more of their own kind if there's junk enough to do so. Although they were fairly common just after ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", as the supply of high-tech components decreased, so did the popularity of Junk Droids.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Behemoth Junk Droids can't be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Behemoth Junk Droid Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e6